  "method_changes": [
    "Borrowed SetValue/Bind copy-construct vacant slots and clone_from occupied slots, preserving address and copy-panic allocation state.",
    "Assign now returns the destination and follows native ascending interleaved block/slot callback order; successful partial copies update count before subsequent throwing copies.",
    "Zero-block constructor permits defined empty operations; explicit Size alias.",
    "Separate legacy base cursor retains native capacity+blocksize exhaustion after scanning allocated blocks, unlike BasicIterator capacity.",
    "Mutable cursor prefix/index/equality and exclusive assignment adapters; const postfix reborrow preserves old position.",
    "Original IteratorFunctions now tests actual cursors; STLIterators now tests conversion/cursor equality instead of substituting value pointer equality."
  ],
  "remaining_partial_contracts": [
    "Native SetValue(index, Value(index)) invokes user self-copy-assignment; Clone::clone_from cannot safely receive aliased Rust references. self_set oracle row is not claimed.",
    "Native deleted copy/move constructors differ from explicit Rust Clone/move extensions; copy_move_traits oracle row is not claimed.",
    "Native mutable iterator shallow copy/postfix aliases require a raw adapter; current postfix returns a const reborrow and mutable assignment exclusively borrows source.",
    "NCollection_SparseArrayBase erased callback storage, CreateItemFunc/DestroyItemFunc/CopyItemFunc, protected fields and Block/getBlock/getItem representation remain unported.",
    "BasicIterator arbitrary container/value template specialization and full compiler method closure remain incomplete.",
    "Existing owned insertion remains a Rust extension, and Option-returning invalid lookup/detached legacy Index=0 replace native exception/undefined behavior.",
    "Throwing destructors and callbacks inspecting intermediate block destruction counts require a separate raw callback layer audit."
  ],
